-- title:
--   Positive finite measure for the compact torus in Z(γ₀)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, $v$ a nonzero prime of its ring of integers $\mathcal O_K$, and $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, where $K_v$ denotes the $v$-adic completion of $K$. Assume $\gamma_0$ is regular semisimple in the sense that $\operatorname{tr}(\gamma_0)^2 - 4\det(\gamma_0)$ is a unit, and that $\gamma_0$ is non-split in the sense that for no $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ do the $(0,1)$ and $(1,0)$ entries of $g^{-1}\gamma_0 g$ both vanish. Let $\nu_T$ be a measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ for the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of its topology, and assume that $\nu_T$ is the pushforward, along the inclusion of the centraliser $Z(\gamma_0) = \mathrm{Centralizer}(\{\gamma_0\})$ with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra, of some Haar measure on $Z(\gamma_0)$. The conclusion is that the set of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ lying in $Z(\gamma_0)$ and satisfying $|\det g|_v = 1$ and $|\operatorname{tr} g|_v \le 1$ (valuations of the determinant and trace of the underlying matrix, taken in the valuation of $K_v$) has $\nu_T$-measure strictly between $0$ and $\infty$.
--
--   The set in question is the compact torus $\mathcal O_E^\times$ inside $Z(\gamma_0) \cong E^\times$, for $E = K_v[\gamma_0]$ the quadratic étale algebra generated by $\gamma_0$; its positivity and finiteness are what make the volume $\theta = \nu_T(T_c)$ a genuine positive real number. It is used in the normalisation of local orbital integrals at a non-split regular semisimple element, being cited by [`AutomorphicForm.measureReal_torusUnits_pos_and_measure_detUnits_lt_top_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.measureReal_torusUnits_pos_and_measure_detUnits_lt_top_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two) and [`AutomorphicForm.mul_measureReal_torusUnits_eq_neg_div_of_forall_isOrbitalIntegral_eq_add_nhds_scalar_of_forall_not_diagonal`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.mul_measureReal_torusUnits_eq_neg_div_of_forall_isOrbitalIntegral_eq_add_nhds_scalar_of_forall_not_diagonal).
